<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Account security | TrackEase</title><jsp:include page="../WEB-INF/ui/head.jsp" /></head><body><jsp:include page="../navbar.jsp" /><main id="main-content" class="shell"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">TrackEase / Account security</span><h1>Account security</h1></div><div data-feature-message role="alert" hidden></div><section class="panel feature-narrow"><h2>Recovery without email.</h2><p>Generate eight private recovery codes now. If you forget your password, use one to recover your account. Generating a set invalidates all previous codes.</p><form data-generate-recovery><div class="field"><label class="form-label" for="currentPassword">Current password</label><input class="form-control" type="password" id="currentPassword" name="password" autocomplete="current-password" required maxlength="1024"></div><label class="field-help d-block mb-3"><input type="checkbox" required> I understand that I must save the new codes privately; they cannot be displayed again.</label><button class="button" type="submit">Generate recovery codes</button></form><div data-recovery-output hidden><p class="alert alert-info mt-3">Save these now. They will not be available after leaving this page.</p><label class="form-label" for="recoveryCodes">Your recovery codes</label><textarea class="form-control recovery-codes" id="recoveryCodes" rows="8" readonly autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"></textarea><button type="button" class="button secondary mt-3" data-download-codes>Download codes</button></div></section></main><jsp:include page="../WEB-INF/ui/footer.jsp" /></body></html>